You open your laptop and gear up for another long day of scanning the crime log and switching tabs between local TV affiliates. It’s only been six-months reporting for The Kalamazoo Citizen, but you’re already sneaking glimpses at LinkedIn during breaks and scheduling interviews during “vacation days.” You got into journalism to keep the public informed and tell meaningful stories, not just rehash whatever the bigger stations are saying. 

