It’s so spammy and clickbaity, classic PR jargon. ECHO, of course, being the flashiest social media startup of the year, run by a stereotypical egomaniac tech guru. Users have a chip implanted in their brain that gives them instantaneous access to social media, news, TV, and messaging all without lifting a finger.

