== openEmail ==
You open the email expecting to see a press release announcing the latest ECHO platform or influencer collab. Instead, a much shorter message awaits:
	
	Dear Chloe,
		
My name is Sam Hereford and I’m an ex-ECHO employee. You can verify this on LinkedIn, Facebook, Forbes, ect. Since I left the company three years ago, I’ve been avidly researching ECHO technology and business practices—I’m deeply concerned about the leadership’s true motives behind the WAVE implant.

I know I’m onto something big. 

The working thesis: ECHO is intentionally manipulating user speech, and thought, using its WAVE neural chip software to serve government interest.

I’m hesitant to say much more over email, or even over the phone, for (hopefully) obvious reasons. 

While I also can’t explain why, you’re the only journalist I trust to break this information. This scoop is newsworthy enough that the national pubs will notice anyway once you put it out there. The story should come from you.

If you’re interested (you should be), reach out on signal. Ford.sam.689

Best,
Sam

