== factory == 
You and Sam coordinate a time to go visit WAVE headquarters in Madison, Wisconsin. He refuses to enter with you (too many bad memories) but sets up interviews with current employees. 

You fly up to Madison, mostly a quaint college town excluding the looming WAVE headquarters on the outskirts. Sam tells you they chose that location to lure in unsuspecting college grads with 100k starting salaries in exchange for 80+ house workweeks. They actually prefer employees with no work experience—anyone who’s ever worked for the traditional corporations (Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp, ect) is blacklisted.

The sprawling offices, collectively known as “campus,” consist of an eclectic collection of building styles. From medieval castles to modern high rises, the architecture has it all.

For whatever reason, it all feels naggingly familiar.

Of course, no employee wants to talk to you during working hours, so you’re here somewhat undercover. You walk through a circus-themed reception room for your hour-long tour of the WAVE campus. You take note of the seemingly endless amenities—free sushi lunches, free dinner for those who stay past 8 p.m., reduced rents for those living within a mile of headquarters, a six-month sabbatical for the (rare) employees who make it past the five-year mark. Where is all this money coming from, you think, and what are they trying to compensate for?

Sam’s contacts are, predictably, busy. Because of their work schedules, you’re forced to pick between three of his suggestions. 

